Our changes to Daniel Anderson's parlay::atomic_shared_ptr internals, applied by
SharedPtr's `make imports` (../../third_party.mk) to copies of upstream's files
(AtomicSharedPtr 3c213ef). Nothing outside the two files below is changed;
ParlayLib is used as is.

details/hazard_pointers.hpp -- folly removed:
  - folly::F14FastSet -> std::unordered_set for the protected-pointer set of the
    reclamation scan (upstream uses only construct-with-bucket-count, insert,
    count, clear and swap, all std::unordered_set API).
  - folly's asymmetric light/heavy fence pair -> a seq_cst thread fence on both
    sides (protect() and cleanup()).
  - <parlay/portability.h> -> "../portability.h": ParlayLib's headers are copied
    into the same parlay/ directory, so no include path is needed.
  - the GCC-only "-Winterference-size" pragmas are guarded from clang.
shared_ptr.hpp -- Harris mark support and include path:
  - get_unmarked_control_block() masks bit 0 of the control-block pointer; the
    reference-count helpers of smart_ptr_base (use_count, increment/decrement
    of the strong and weak counts) go through it, so a shared_ptr whose control
    block carries the list's delete mark (lock_free_shared_ptr/atomic_shared_ptr.hpp
    shared_ptr_type::set_mark()) can be copied and destroyed. Not covered:
    weak_ptr's converting constructors (weak_ptr<T2> to weak_ptr<T>), which call
    the counts directly; nothing here uses parlay::weak_ptr.
  - <parlay/alloc.h> -> "alloc.h" (ParlayLib's allocator, same directory).
  - [[maybe_unused]] on control_block_inplace::operator new's size argument,
    which only an assert reads: unused under -DNDEBUG, and the builds use -Werror.

